From: Janek210102j <janek210102j@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:29:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Merch page synced daily from Bandcamp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New Merch page (/#/merch, in the menu and footer): cards with photo,
  type, price and sold-out state; each opens the item on Bandcamp, where
  people order. Sold-out items go last. Empty state links to Bandcamp.
- scripts/merch-sync: reads https://discardedband.bandcamp.com/merch and
  writes the items to Firestore (site_content/merch). Only Bandcamp links
  and Bandcamp images are kept. If Bandcamp is down or its layout changes,
  the saved list is left alone and the error is recorded instead.
  Parser tested against the real page markup (fixtures/merch-page.html).
- GitHub Actions workflow runs it every day and on demand; needs the
  FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT secret (see scripts/merch-sync/README.md).
- Admin → Merch: last sync time, errors, a link to run the sync, which
  items show on the site, and the intro text.
- Navbar fits seven links: centred over the bar from 1500px, next to the
  logo below that; tighter phone menu on short screens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
